From: AudioSmith
Subject: [PATCH] ui/editor: keep what soft wraps shape; a real budget

Since soft wraps shape the lines they break (the patch before), every
layout of a line shaped it again, with no cache: opening or resizing a
long text took 60-120 ms in a frame, a keystroke 1-4 ms, and
measureWraps' 4 ms budget did not hold, as it measured 400 lines near
the anchor without looking at the time and the others 256 at a time.

wrapCache keeps, per displayed line, by its text, the advances of its
characters (for the style and scale) and its breaks (for the wrap width
too), and the widths of the rows fitRow shaped, by their text. An edit
makes new texts, which miss, and leaves those of the other lines, which
hit: typing reshapes the line typed in. Another wrap width keeps the
advances; another style or scale forgets all; lines no layout used go
once the cache holds many more than the text. Rows shaped for lines laid
out to paint go into the frame's layouts, which paint them.

measureWraps measures the lines that show from the anchor whatever the
budget, so what shows is right at once, then those around it and the
rest within the budget, looking at the time every 4 lines.

Linux (Pango), 200,000 characters at 640 DIPs: the first frame after a
resize 62-108 ms -> 4-5 ms, a keystroke 1.2/3.4 ms -> 0.2-0.3/1.4 ms,
measuring all again at another width 63-123 ms -> 5-34 ms, now spread
over frames. Tests: TestWrapCacheFollowsEdits (cached wraps are those
measured afresh, after an edit and at another width) and
TestMeasureWrapsKeepsItsBudget; TestWrappedRowsFitTheWrapWidth passes.
---
